---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
---
<BaseLayout title="Community cost voting privacy — Vetlas" description="See which visit-cost information is public, how a browser vote is remembered and how to change or remove it.">
 <div class="container policy-page">
  <Breadcrumbs items={[{name:"Home",href:"/"},{name:"Privacy",href:"/privacy/"}]}/>
  <header class="page-head"><p class="kicker">Community cost voting</p><h1>Where your vote goes</h1><p>A visit-cost vote contains the range you chose, an optional exact total and the submission time. You can vote without giving your name or medical records.</p></header>
  <div class="policy-columns">
   <section><h2>On your browser</h2><p>A first-party HTTP-only cookie remembers this browser for up to a year. One current vote per browser per facility counts. Changing your vote replaces the previous one. Use “Remove my vote” to delete it before clearing cookies.</p></section>
   <section><h2>In the voting database</h2><p>Vetlas stores a salted hash of the identifier for each facility. A separate salted daily hash of the network address limits repeat submissions. Daily limit records are cleared on the next write after that day. Raw IP addresses are excluded from this database. Hosting infrastructure may keep operational logs.</p></section>
   <section><h2>On the facility page</h2><p>Visitors see counts by cost range, an estimated average and the number of exact totals. Individual records stay private. These are self-reported costs. Votes older than 365 days are excluded and removed when results for that facility are requested.</p><a href="/methodology/">How cost estimates work →</a></section>
   <section><h2>When you use another service</h2><p>Photos are served by Vetlas. Following a credit link visits the original host. Map previews load Google Maps, and the optional Places integration can be configured separately. The review form prepares an email draft separately from cost voting.</p><a href="/review/">Open the review form →</a></section>
  </div>
 </div>
</BaseLayout>
